1
00:00:01,042 --> 00:00:02,625
[intense music]

2
00:00:07,083 --> 00:00:09,542
[metal clanking]

3
00:00:13,417 --> 00:00:14,792
[sizzles]

4
00:00:14,875 --> 00:00:18,542
Ah, brother.
Back sooner than expected.

5
00:00:19,625 --> 00:00:21,000
How went the south?

6
00:00:21,083 --> 00:00:22,542
How do you think it went?

7
00:00:22,625 --> 00:00:24,750
Everything below
the Jagged Divide

8
00:00:24,833 --> 00:00:27,708
has either submitted
to the army of the Five,

9
00:00:27,792 --> 00:00:31,500
or was razed to the ground
by the power of Shatterspin.

10
00:00:31,583 --> 00:00:34,667
But don't take my word for it.

11
00:00:36,167 --> 00:00:40,333
[scoffs]
Who's this pathetic beast?

12
00:00:40,417 --> 00:00:43,083
A souvenir I collected
on my travels.

13
00:00:43,167 --> 00:00:45,583
Believe it or not,
there's a tribe down there

14
00:00:45,667 --> 00:00:49,333
who considers this to be
a great champion.

15
00:00:49,417 --> 00:00:53,667
Speak, wretch.
Tell them of my glory.

16
00:00:53,750 --> 00:00:56,458
Of our glory.

17
00:00:56,542 --> 00:00:58,167
[growls]

18
00:00:59,417 --> 00:01:01,167
How could you?

19
00:01:01,250 --> 00:01:04,417
The evil you've done
to my people!

20
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:09,042
[laughs]

21
00:01:10,917 --> 00:01:12,833
Listen, whelp,

22
00:01:12,917 --> 00:01:16,000
what you call evil,
we know as strength.

23
00:01:16,083 --> 00:01:18,542
And what was done
to your people,

24
00:01:18,625 --> 00:01:20,708
done across the Wyldness,

25
00:01:20,792 --> 00:01:25,000
will soon be done
to every realm of creation.

26
00:01:26,292 --> 00:01:29,000
Prepare, my fellow conquerors.

27
00:01:29,083 --> 00:01:31,792
Soon, we walk the realms.

28
00:01:31,875 --> 00:01:33,708
[dragons roaring]

29
00:01:33,792 --> 00:01:37,125
Hm. Something's coming
from the East.

30
00:01:46,458 --> 00:01:48,167
Don't worry, my brother.

31
00:01:48,250 --> 00:01:50,333
It will not be long now.

32
00:01:50,417 --> 00:01:52,375
He must be crushed.

33
00:01:52,458 --> 00:01:54,417
Oh, he will be.

34
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:57,292
Just as his ancestors
once were.

35
00:01:57,375 --> 00:02:00,083
And the long-delayed plans

36
00:02:00,167 --> 00:02:05,833
of the Forbidden Five
will finally unfold.

37
00:02:05,917 --> 00:02:08,542
♪ Lost in the unknown
So much to see ♪

38
00:02:08,625 --> 00:02:11,542
♪ Together we will rise! ♪

39
00:02:11,625 --> 00:02:14,750
♪ We fight ♪

40
00:02:14,833 --> 00:02:18,125
♪ Be a ninja
For what's right! ♪

41
00:02:19,333 --> 00:02:21,000
[flames roaring]

42
00:02:21,083 --> 00:02:23,167
[light music]

43
00:02:27,042 --> 00:02:28,917
-Look out!
-Ugh!

44
00:02:32,208 --> 00:02:35,000
Ugh. I don't care
for being jostled about

45
00:02:35,083 --> 00:02:36,333
like a sack of beets.

46
00:02:38,292 --> 00:02:40,708
But I really don't care
for getting crushed.

47
00:02:40,792 --> 00:02:42,458
So, thank you,

48
00:02:42,542 --> 00:02:46,167
for your timely intervention,
young lady.

49
00:02:46,250 --> 00:02:47,583
You know us Ninja,

50
00:02:47,667 --> 00:02:49,750
we're all about helping others,

51
00:02:49,833 --> 00:02:51,458
is what they keep telling me.

52
00:02:51,542 --> 00:02:55,458
I wonder what could have caused
that brick to fall like that.

53
00:02:55,542 --> 00:02:57,917
Meh, sometimes bricks fall.

54
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,625
Probably no one set that up
as a prank or anything.

55
00:03:00,708 --> 00:03:03,500
Hey-hey, bet
an important guy like you

56
00:03:03,583 --> 00:03:06,042
has major urgent stuff
to do, huh?

57
00:03:06,125 --> 00:03:10,417
Yes, my duties
are quite indispensable.

58
00:03:10,500 --> 00:03:12,458
I'd better get on with them.

59
00:03:14,625 --> 00:03:16,125
Ha. Switched with a fake

60
00:03:16,208 --> 00:03:18,667
and that old grump
never even noticed.

61
00:03:18,750 --> 00:03:21,417
The being-crushed-by-a-brick
prank works again!

62
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:23,458
The Lava-Tides used to love it.

63
00:03:23,542 --> 00:03:26,750
And it rarely ever
decimated their entire village.

64
00:03:27,708 --> 00:03:30,000
There's gotta be some clues
to Bleckt's crimes in--

65
00:03:30,083 --> 00:03:31,417
[gasps] Huh?

66
00:03:31,500 --> 00:03:33,208
What language is this?

67
00:03:33,292 --> 00:03:34,750
It's gibberish!

68
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:40,542
Master Wu?! Is it--

69
00:03:40,625 --> 00:03:42,000
Is it really you?

70
00:03:48,375 --> 00:03:49,750
[doors bang open]

71
00:03:57,958 --> 00:04:00,250
Master Wu, where'd you go?

72
00:04:00,333 --> 00:04:01,875
Cole, look!

73
00:04:01,958 --> 00:04:03,333
[mysterious music]

74
00:04:03,417 --> 00:04:05,042
[Cole]
More Portal Gates?

75
00:04:06,083 --> 00:04:08,250
[Arin]
Is that the Cloud Kingdom?

76
00:04:08,333 --> 00:04:09,958
Guess we know
where that gate goes.

77
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:15,250
[Cole]
That looks like Mysterium.

78
00:04:15,333 --> 00:04:17,542
And there's
the Land of Lost Things.

79
00:04:19,375 --> 00:04:22,083
And Ninjago, our home.

80
00:04:22,167 --> 00:04:24,667
[Cole] ...fourteen,
fifteen, sixteen.

81
00:04:24,750 --> 00:04:27,875
Huh, one gate
for each of the realms?

82
00:04:27,958 --> 00:04:29,500
-[Master Wu] Yes.
-[Cole, Arin gasp]

83
00:04:31,292 --> 00:04:32,833
Master Wu?

84
00:04:32,917 --> 00:04:34,833
It's really you, isn't it?

85
00:04:34,917 --> 00:04:36,875
Yes.

86
00:04:36,958 --> 00:04:38,417
We've missed you so much!

87
00:04:38,500 --> 00:04:40,042
What happened to you
in the Merge?

88
00:04:40,125 --> 00:04:42,000
Are you-- are you departed?

89
00:04:42,083 --> 00:04:44,583
And why are you
suddenly appearing now?!

90
00:04:44,667 --> 00:04:46,542
Horns.

91
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:53,292
Horns? He doesn't mean...

92
00:04:55,208 --> 00:04:56,583
[Cole]
He does.

93
00:04:56,667 --> 00:04:59,208
[Arin] The crowns
of the murdered dragons!

94
00:05:00,458 --> 00:05:01,833
Wait, Master Wu!

95
00:05:01,917 --> 00:05:04,833
Ras told me
you caused the Merge.

96
00:05:04,917 --> 00:05:06,250
Did you?

97
00:05:06,333 --> 00:05:08,042
Arin, Ras is a liar.

98
00:05:08,125 --> 00:05:10,667
There's no way
Master Wu would ever--

99
00:05:10,750 --> 00:05:11,875
I need to know!

100
00:05:11,958 --> 00:05:14,208
Did you cause the Merge?

101
00:05:15,833 --> 00:05:16,875
Yes.

102
00:05:16,958 --> 00:05:18,000
Huh?

103
00:05:19,042 --> 00:05:21,917
[whooshing]

104
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:25,500
That-- that can't be right.

105
00:05:25,583 --> 00:05:27,750
Everything I thought I knew...

106
00:05:27,833 --> 00:05:29,583
it's all wrong.

107
00:05:30,625 --> 00:05:33,542
Okay. I'm trying
for twice as far this time.

108
00:05:33,625 --> 00:05:35,583
And-- Poof!

109
00:05:35,667 --> 00:05:38,833
[coughing]

110
00:05:38,917 --> 00:05:40,875
How does Cinder live like this?

111
00:05:40,958 --> 00:05:43,333
-[coughs]
-Hydration recommended.

112
00:05:44,583 --> 00:05:47,792
[coughs] Thanks, Zane.

113
00:05:47,875 --> 00:05:50,958
So, did I get twice as far?

114
00:05:51,042 --> 00:05:54,583
You actually appear to
have gone slightly backwards.

115
00:05:56,542 --> 00:05:59,667
Argh! That jerk Cinder
made it look so easy,

116
00:05:59,750 --> 00:06:01,458
but nothing's working!

117
00:06:01,542 --> 00:06:03,167
I can't Quake like Frak,

118
00:06:03,250 --> 00:06:05,417
or use Elemental Reflex
like Zur.

119
00:06:05,500 --> 00:06:06,667
I have their powers,

120
00:06:06,750 --> 00:06:08,875
why can't I be
like any of them?

121
00:06:08,958 --> 00:06:11,083
I think that's the problem,
Sora.

122
00:06:11,167 --> 00:06:13,083
You're trying to be like them.

123
00:06:13,167 --> 00:06:15,500
Uh, yeah! What else can I do?

124
00:06:15,583 --> 00:06:16,792
You can be you.

125
00:06:16,875 --> 00:06:19,167
Being me isn't great
right now.

126
00:06:19,250 --> 00:06:20,750
My best friend hates me.

127
00:06:20,833 --> 00:06:23,250
My Spinjitzu
still won't spin-jitz.

128
00:06:23,333 --> 00:06:25,333
And an evil loser
from ancient times

129
00:06:25,417 --> 00:06:27,958
is about to trash me
in front of a live audience.

130
00:06:28,042 --> 00:06:32,417
Sora, I've seen you do things
no one else could ever do.

131
00:06:32,500 --> 00:06:34,417
Stop trying to
use Elemental Powers

132
00:06:34,500 --> 00:06:36,000
the way everyone else did.

133
00:06:36,083 --> 00:06:38,708
Think of how only Sora
would use them.

134
00:06:38,792 --> 00:06:40,167
And how's that?

135
00:06:40,250 --> 00:06:41,500
I don't know.

136
00:06:41,583 --> 00:06:43,542
But I look forward
to finding out.

137
00:06:44,583 --> 00:06:46,458
I think the time
for coaching is over.

138
00:06:48,667 --> 00:06:51,042
Be right back. There's
someone I need to talk to.

139
00:06:52,167 --> 00:06:53,250
I got your note.

140
00:06:53,333 --> 00:06:54,792
What note?

141
00:06:54,875 --> 00:06:56,833
Look, I don't understand

142
00:06:56,917 --> 00:06:58,542
what's going on with you,
Jordana,

143
00:06:58,625 --> 00:07:01,250
but I want to tell you,
I'm sorry.

144
00:07:01,333 --> 00:07:02,625
I didn't remember you

145
00:07:02,708 --> 00:07:04,292
from when we
were in school together.

146
00:07:04,375 --> 00:07:07,417
I know that upset you and
made you feel unimportant.

147
00:07:07,500 --> 00:07:09,500
Me and my friend Arin
have been--

148
00:07:09,583 --> 00:07:11,417
I just--

149
00:07:11,500 --> 00:07:14,708
I wish I hadn't been
so wrapped up in my own stuff.

150
00:07:14,792 --> 00:07:16,958
I wish I'd remembered you.

151
00:07:17,042 --> 00:07:19,333
School was a really lonely
time in my life,

152
00:07:19,417 --> 00:07:21,500
and I could have used a friend.

153
00:07:21,583 --> 00:07:23,125
Maybe we both could have.

154
00:07:23,208 --> 00:07:26,000
So, I'm sorry.

155
00:07:26,083 --> 00:07:28,000
[scoffs] Pathetic.

156
00:07:31,958 --> 00:07:35,500
What is this? Clown language?!
Ugh!

157
00:07:37,708 --> 00:07:41,333
This language is Devonian,
like me.

158
00:07:41,417 --> 00:07:44,875
Master Zur?
Wait, you can talk?

159
00:07:44,958 --> 00:07:48,333
Of course. Why would you
think otherwise?

160
00:07:48,417 --> 00:07:50,333
I've never heard you
say anything.

161
00:07:50,417 --> 00:07:52,417
Just grunts and harsh looks.

162
00:07:52,500 --> 00:07:54,750
Plus, I'd expect your voice
to sound more...

163
00:07:54,833 --> 00:07:57,083
I don't know, evil-ish?

164
00:07:57,167 --> 00:08:00,000
My kind are extremely shy.

165
00:08:00,083 --> 00:08:02,000
But because of our appearance,

166
00:08:02,083 --> 00:08:04,625
there are those who
make false assumptions

167
00:08:04,708 --> 00:08:07,375
and spread rumors about us.

168
00:08:07,458 --> 00:08:11,375
Devonians are renowned
for our kindness, actually.

169
00:08:11,458 --> 00:08:13,375
So, you can actually read this?

170
00:08:13,458 --> 00:08:17,667
Yes, it is a ancient form
of my language,

171
00:08:17,750 --> 00:08:20,500
from the early days
of our history.

172
00:08:20,583 --> 00:08:23,833
It must still be used here
in the City of Temples.

173
00:08:23,917 --> 00:08:28,125
I can help you translate
this book, if you would like.

174
00:08:29,333 --> 00:08:30,750
[crowd cheering]

175
00:08:30,833 --> 00:08:35,083
Ah. Today's just
another normal day, I guess?

176
00:08:35,167 --> 00:08:38,500
Wrong! Today is
the most important day

177
00:08:38,583 --> 00:08:41,625
in the history of all time
and forever!

178
00:08:41,708 --> 00:08:43,875
The final championship

179
00:08:43,958 --> 00:08:47,417
of the greatest Tournament ever
Gamesmastered!

180
00:08:47,500 --> 00:08:51,083
-[cheering]
-[fireworks exploding]

181
00:08:56,667 --> 00:08:58,292
In this corner, Sora,

182
00:08:58,375 --> 00:09:01,708
coached by her Ninja teacher,
Master Lloyd Garmadon!

183
00:09:01,792 --> 00:09:03,667
[cheering]

184
00:09:07,458 --> 00:09:09,500
And in this corner, Nokt,

185
00:09:09,583 --> 00:09:12,750
coached by his commander,
Lord Ras of the Wyldness.

186
00:09:12,833 --> 00:09:13,833
[cheering]

187
00:09:13,917 --> 00:09:15,375
With this final match,

188
00:09:15,458 --> 00:09:18,125
the Tournament will end
just like it started:

189
00:09:18,208 --> 00:09:19,833
One-on-one combat!

190
00:09:19,917 --> 00:09:22,958
Last one standing wins it all!

191
00:09:27,917 --> 00:09:30,917
Time to go "be myself,"
or whatever.

192
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:33,625
Let the game begin!

193
00:09:33,708 --> 00:09:35,083
[cheering]

194
00:09:36,417 --> 00:09:40,292
[grunts] Ah!

195
00:09:41,417 --> 00:09:42,417
Ugh.

196
00:09:42,500 --> 00:09:45,333
[gasps, murmurs]

197
00:09:45,417 --> 00:09:48,958
I have no idea how you even
made it this far, girl.

198
00:09:49,042 --> 00:09:53,333
But I promise you, you've
never faced anyone like me.

199
00:09:54,792 --> 00:09:56,625
I faced parents like you.

200
00:09:56,708 --> 00:09:59,042
I faced a whole realm like you.

201
00:09:59,125 --> 00:10:03,542
[yawns] Is your sob story
over yet?

202
00:10:06,375 --> 00:10:08,208
Straight for the Shatterspin,
folks!

203
00:10:08,292 --> 00:10:11,000
Looks like this match might end
before it really gets started.

204
00:10:14,875 --> 00:10:16,250
A little ice?

205
00:10:16,333 --> 00:10:17,750
Please.

206
00:10:19,042 --> 00:10:21,917
[rumbling]

207
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:23,583
I do not understand.

208
00:10:23,667 --> 00:10:25,958
Why is she combining
Frak's quake power

209
00:10:26,042 --> 00:10:27,667
with my ice power?

210
00:10:30,292 --> 00:10:32,667
[pounding]

211
00:10:32,750 --> 00:10:35,292
And now Elemental Reflex power?

212
00:10:35,375 --> 00:10:37,542
I don't know,
but it looks like something

213
00:10:37,625 --> 00:10:39,000
no one else would try.

214
00:10:46,583 --> 00:10:48,375
[explosion]

215
00:10:48,458 --> 00:10:49,917
Aah!

216
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:53,083
Whoa! Somehow,
Sora created a barrier

217
00:10:53,167 --> 00:10:56,333
that vibrated exactly counter
to Shatterspin.

218
00:10:56,417 --> 00:10:58,625
Can you believe how good
my games are?

219
00:10:58,708 --> 00:11:00,875
Finish this, you fool!

220
00:11:00,958 --> 00:11:03,125
Throw everything else
you've got at her!

221
00:11:05,625 --> 00:11:06,792
[explosion]

222
00:11:06,875 --> 00:11:08,417
[grunts, coughs]

223
00:11:10,667 --> 00:11:12,083
[zaps]

224
00:11:16,833 --> 00:11:18,167
[grunts]

225
00:11:18,250 --> 00:11:21,167
Power after power,
blow after blow!

226
00:11:21,250 --> 00:11:24,083
Are you not entertained?!

227
00:11:24,167 --> 00:11:25,458
[cheering]

228
00:11:26,833 --> 00:11:28,167
Lloyd, we found them!

229
00:11:28,250 --> 00:11:29,542
Found what?

230
00:11:29,625 --> 00:11:31,458
The missing horns
of the dead dragons.

231
00:11:31,542 --> 00:11:33,042
Cole and I found them.

232
00:11:33,125 --> 00:11:35,458
-Where?
-They're in another Monastery.

233
00:11:35,542 --> 00:11:37,875
Jordana gave us a message
that led us to them.

234
00:11:37,958 --> 00:11:40,958
Jordana? Does that prove
Ras is behind all this?

235
00:11:41,042 --> 00:11:43,542
I think so. We know
he was meeting with Bleckt.

236
00:11:43,625 --> 00:11:46,292
But I don't know what he plans
to do with the horns.

237
00:11:46,375 --> 00:11:48,167
He's determined to get control

238
00:11:48,250 --> 00:11:50,125
of all the Elemental Powers
in this game.

239
00:11:50,208 --> 00:11:52,000
He's gotta be planning
to use the powers

240
00:11:52,083 --> 00:11:54,542
and the horns together
to get to the Source Dragons.

241
00:11:54,625 --> 00:11:57,042
You and Zane, go back and
get those horns out of there.

242
00:11:57,125 --> 00:11:59,000
Ras can't use 'em
if he can't find them.

243
00:11:59,083 --> 00:12:01,833
I'll stay to coach Sora.
She's gotta win this game.

244
00:12:01,917 --> 00:12:03,958
There's something else.

245
00:12:04,042 --> 00:12:07,042
We saw the ghost of Master Wu
in the Monastery.

246
00:12:07,125 --> 00:12:08,167
What?

247
00:12:08,250 --> 00:12:10,250
He said he caused the Merge.

248
00:12:10,333 --> 00:12:13,542
What? That-- that's impossible.

249
00:12:13,625 --> 00:12:15,000
Lloyd, it's true.

250
00:12:16,583 --> 00:12:18,292
[Sora yells]

251
00:12:18,375 --> 00:12:19,958
We can't let Ras win.

252
00:12:20,042 --> 00:12:22,333
Arin, Zane, get those horns
out of there!

253
00:12:23,958 --> 00:12:25,125
Come on, Zane.

254
00:12:27,167 --> 00:12:29,292
[menacing music]

255
00:12:33,833 --> 00:12:36,500
[both grunting with effort]

256
00:12:36,583 --> 00:12:38,750
Nokt should have won by now.

257
00:12:38,833 --> 00:12:40,833
He cannot fail me.

258
00:12:40,917 --> 00:12:42,792
[grunting]

259
00:12:42,875 --> 00:12:44,208
[yells]

260
00:12:45,250 --> 00:12:46,417
[grunts]

261
00:12:46,500 --> 00:12:47,583
[yells]

262
00:12:47,667 --> 00:12:49,042
Ugh.

263
00:12:49,583 --> 00:12:53,042
There's nothing you can do
that I can't do better, kid!

264
00:12:53,125 --> 00:12:54,833
Sora! Remember,

265
00:12:54,917 --> 00:12:57,125
if you can't outfight him,
outsmart him!

266
00:12:57,208 --> 00:12:59,042
What's that thing?

267
00:13:00,333 --> 00:13:02,167
Probably not a fashion choice.

268
00:13:07,292 --> 00:13:10,375
You think you defeat me
with a bumble-bee?

269
00:13:10,458 --> 00:13:11,917
[buzzes]

270
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:13,667
-[grunts]
-[zapping]

271
00:13:14,958 --> 00:13:16,500
-[grunts]
-[zapping]

272
00:13:16,583 --> 00:13:18,333
Looks like it's all over,
folks!

273
00:13:18,417 --> 00:13:20,375
[cheering]

274
00:13:20,458 --> 00:13:21,500
[grunts]

275
00:13:23,292 --> 00:13:24,708
Ugh!

276
00:13:24,792 --> 00:13:26,042
Wait. What?

277
00:13:26,125 --> 00:13:28,583
Oh! Lucky for Nokt,

278
00:13:28,667 --> 00:13:30,792
the arena suddenly shifts
in his favor!

279
00:13:30,875 --> 00:13:33,333
Expect the unexpected, folks!

280
00:13:33,417 --> 00:13:34,792
We didn't program
the floor to move

281
00:13:34,875 --> 00:13:36,042
in the final match, did we?

282
00:13:36,125 --> 00:13:37,792
Not sure.

283
00:13:37,875 --> 00:13:40,667
But isn't giving the crowd
high drama what you want?

284
00:13:40,750 --> 00:13:43,167
Well, yeah, I guess.

285
00:13:46,792 --> 00:13:47,833
[grunts]

286
00:13:49,125 --> 00:13:50,250
[grunts]

287
00:13:50,333 --> 00:13:53,000
[both grunting with effort]

288
00:13:55,083 --> 00:13:56,167
Ah!

289
00:13:58,792 --> 00:14:00,125
[Roby]
Coming back from behind,

290
00:14:00,208 --> 00:14:01,500
Nokt hits Sora with Shatterspin

291
00:14:01,583 --> 00:14:03,042
before she can react!

292
00:14:03,125 --> 00:14:05,917
And with only one player
left standing,

293
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:08,375
this tournament
has a new champion.

294
00:14:08,458 --> 00:14:11,042
Nokt is the winner!

295
00:14:11,125 --> 00:14:13,250
[crowd cheering]

296
00:14:46,083 --> 00:14:47,833
[fireworks exploding]

297
00:14:47,917 --> 00:14:49,375
[cheering]

298
00:14:54,833 --> 00:14:56,833
You were amazing out there.

299
00:14:56,917 --> 00:14:58,333
Better than me.

300
00:14:58,417 --> 00:15:01,458
Than nearly every
Elemental Master ever.

301
00:15:01,542 --> 00:15:04,583
But Ras is gonna have control
of all the powers now.

302
00:15:04,667 --> 00:15:07,167
Let's hope Arin and Zane
manage to get those horns.

303
00:15:07,250 --> 00:15:10,917
And so, for the final time
in these games,

304
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:14,125
I'll transfer powers
with the Element Cup.

305
00:15:14,208 --> 00:15:15,958
Whoop-whoop!

306
00:15:18,875 --> 00:15:21,542
And now, the Victory Ceremony
to declare

307
00:15:21,625 --> 00:15:25,083
a new Champion of the Sources!

308
00:15:25,167 --> 00:15:27,125
[crowd cheering]

309
00:15:28,250 --> 00:15:29,292
[Wyldfyre]
Objection!

310
00:15:29,375 --> 00:15:31,125
[crowd gasps]

311
00:15:34,917 --> 00:15:38,500
What? You can't object
to the victory ceremony.

312
00:15:38,583 --> 00:15:42,125
You clearly know nothing
of the ancient rites!

313
00:15:42,208 --> 00:15:44,458
Okay, then, "point of order"?

314
00:15:44,542 --> 00:15:46,000
That's not a thing either!

315
00:15:46,083 --> 00:15:47,458
Uh, "time out"?

316
00:15:47,542 --> 00:15:49,167
No, no, no!

317
00:15:49,250 --> 00:15:52,000
These games have been rigged!

318
00:15:52,083 --> 00:15:53,917
-[crowd gasps]
-What?

319
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:56,083
-That's so unfair.
-I don't understand.

320
00:15:57,208 --> 00:15:59,958
[gasps] Vile slander!

321
00:16:00,042 --> 00:16:01,875
How dare you impugn the honor

322
00:16:01,958 --> 00:16:04,000
of the age-old
Tournament of Sources!

323
00:16:04,083 --> 00:16:05,625
For shame!

324
00:16:05,708 --> 00:16:08,375
I dare 'cause
I've got your ledger!

325
00:16:08,458 --> 00:16:12,292
And I can read it,
thanks to my new best-bud, Zur!

326
00:16:12,375 --> 00:16:14,958
[growls] What?

327
00:16:15,042 --> 00:16:17,375
The menu from the banquet?

328
00:16:17,458 --> 00:16:20,792
The ol' swapped-with-a-menu
prank! Classic!

329
00:16:20,875 --> 00:16:24,208
Bleckt here is such
a stickler for ledgers,

330
00:16:24,292 --> 00:16:27,542
he kept detailed notes
on everything about the games,

331
00:16:27,625 --> 00:16:30,083
including his own crimes.

332
00:16:30,167 --> 00:16:32,792
Like him conspiring with Ras!

333
00:16:32,875 --> 00:16:36,333
[gasps, murmurs]

334
00:16:39,042 --> 00:16:41,292
It's all here. Check it out!

335
00:16:46,542 --> 00:16:48,042
Bleckt sent the attack bots

336
00:16:48,125 --> 00:16:50,583
to get rid of Ras's
strongest competition:

337
00:16:51,833 --> 00:16:54,833
us Ninja and Zur.

338
00:16:54,917 --> 00:16:56,917
He even sent a fake one
against Ras

339
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:58,625
to throw off suspicions.

340
00:16:58,708 --> 00:17:00,667
Bleckt's been
rigging the games!

341
00:17:00,750 --> 00:17:02,458
Nothing too obvious,

342
00:17:02,542 --> 00:17:05,042
but always slightly in favor
of Ras' team.

343
00:17:11,167 --> 00:17:14,292
It's true. It's all in here.

344
00:17:14,375 --> 00:17:15,833
He's the reason the Ninja

345
00:17:15,917 --> 00:17:18,292
didn't get their invites
in the first place.

346
00:17:18,375 --> 00:17:20,083
And Zeatrix was actually right,

347
00:17:20,167 --> 00:17:22,542
Uncle Bleckt was trying
to sideline her.

348
00:17:22,625 --> 00:17:24,125
The honor of the games

349
00:17:24,208 --> 00:17:26,792
is like you're whole thing,
Uncle B.

350
00:17:26,875 --> 00:17:29,208
What would make you
do something like this?

351
00:17:29,292 --> 00:17:31,333
Because of you!

352
00:17:31,417 --> 00:17:35,292
You simpleton!
You infantile half-wit!

353
00:17:35,375 --> 00:17:38,167
When my stupid brother
put you in charge,

354
00:17:38,250 --> 00:17:39,958
I knew you'd ruin the games

355
00:17:40,042 --> 00:17:42,542
with all your zang-toot ideas!

356
00:17:42,625 --> 00:17:46,792
It was the only way to
save the games from total ruin!

357
00:17:46,875 --> 00:17:50,250
Once I helped Ras win,
he'd get rid of you.

358
00:17:50,333 --> 00:17:53,292
And then, I would be
the new Gamesmaster,

359
00:17:53,375 --> 00:17:56,667
and dignity would be restored!

360
00:17:56,750 --> 00:17:59,375
First of all,
it's "stang-zoot."

361
00:17:59,458 --> 00:18:03,917
Uncle Bleckt, you are mega,
reverse, negative stang-zoot!

362
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:06,583
[boos, yelling]

363
00:18:06,667 --> 00:18:08,792
[clears throat]
In light of this,

364
00:18:08,875 --> 00:18:11,708
I declare the Victory Ceremony
canceled.

365
00:18:11,792 --> 00:18:12,917
Security!

366
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:14,625
[warbles]

367
00:18:14,708 --> 00:18:18,292
In light of that,
I un-cancel it!

368
00:18:21,833 --> 00:18:23,667
[building yell]

369
00:18:25,708 --> 00:18:27,917
[gasps]

370
00:18:32,042 --> 00:18:35,250
[grunting]

371
00:18:42,083 --> 00:18:46,333
Finally. The powers
I've always deserved!

372
00:18:46,417 --> 00:18:49,208
Good. Time for
the next phase of the plan.

373
00:18:49,292 --> 00:18:52,375
Actually, change of plans.

374
00:18:52,458 --> 00:18:55,667
I don't work for you anymore,
Ras.

375
00:18:58,542 --> 00:19:00,375
[grumbles, gasps]

376
00:19:00,458 --> 00:19:04,250
There's many things
I've come to hate about you.

377
00:19:04,333 --> 00:19:07,583
One of them is how clever
you think you are.

378
00:19:07,667 --> 00:19:10,708
You put a technological
control collar on me,

379
00:19:10,792 --> 00:19:15,375
then you sent me to fight the
Elemental Master of Technology?

380
00:19:15,458 --> 00:19:18,625
He is kind of slow
on the uptake,

381
00:19:18,708 --> 00:19:20,750
isn't he, brother?

382
00:19:20,833 --> 00:19:22,042
"Brother"?

383
00:19:23,125 --> 00:19:25,917
Rox of the Forbidden Five?

384
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:27,625
[Jordana/Rox]
Nokt's physical body

385
00:19:27,708 --> 00:19:29,583
escaped the Nether Space
that day.

386
00:19:29,667 --> 00:19:33,125
But you never realized
my soul escaped

387
00:19:33,208 --> 00:19:36,125
to the nearest form
I could find.

388
00:19:37,167 --> 00:19:39,792
Not the body
I would have picked,

389
00:19:39,875 --> 00:19:42,375
but good enough
for my brother and I

390
00:19:42,458 --> 00:19:44,875
to hunt some dragons.

391
00:19:51,333 --> 00:19:53,417
[growls]

392
00:19:56,542 --> 00:19:57,542
[roars]

393
00:19:57,625 --> 00:19:59,042
[clangs]

394
00:20:07,083 --> 00:20:08,833
Dragons?

395
00:20:08,917 --> 00:20:11,333
Ras, you really didn't know?

396
00:20:11,417 --> 00:20:13,292
Why did you kill
those three dragons?

397
00:20:13,375 --> 00:20:14,875
They did nothing to you.

398
00:20:14,958 --> 00:20:16,750
For the crowns, of course.

399
00:20:16,833 --> 00:20:18,625
With enough Dragon Ivory,

400
00:20:18,708 --> 00:20:21,250
and a multitude
of Elemental Powers...

401
00:20:21,333 --> 00:20:23,542
we don't need
a Blood Moon ritual

402
00:20:23,625 --> 00:20:26,708
to bring back the rest
of the Forbidden Five!

403
00:20:26,792 --> 00:20:30,583
[roars]

404
00:20:30,667 --> 00:20:33,458
You'll do no such thing.

405
00:20:33,542 --> 00:20:35,292
[intense music]

406
00:20:35,375 --> 00:20:39,083
[crowd chatters worriedly]

407
00:20:49,208 --> 00:20:51,542
[bongs]

408
00:20:55,583 --> 00:20:58,250
You will go with me
to the Cauldron of Realms

409
00:20:58,333 --> 00:21:00,500
and complete my Master's will,

410
00:21:00,583 --> 00:21:02,917
or you will be crushed.

411
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:05,750
[laughs] Oh, Ras.

412
00:21:05,833 --> 00:21:09,292
Did you forget where
you got those masks from?

413
00:21:09,375 --> 00:21:11,458
Did you forget
who created them?

414
00:21:15,708 --> 00:21:19,042
And you've barely even
scratched the surface

415
00:21:19,125 --> 00:21:21,583
of their true powers.

416
00:21:23,042 --> 00:21:25,667
[worried chatter]

417
00:21:36,333 --> 00:21:38,000
Finish them!

418
00:21:38,083 --> 00:21:40,667
Every single one of them!

419
00:21:44,917 --> 00:21:46,500
[intense music]

